#. W_RAM
#, python-brace-format
msgid "One job needs about {need_gb} GB of RAM and {free_gb} GB is free, so jobs run one at a time and may still swap. Close other programs, or shrink the model (region.expand_h, mesh.n in project.json)."
msgstr ""

#. E_DT_FLOOR
#, python-brace-format
msgid "openEMS's timestep {dt} s is below {floor} × the reference {ref} s, set by the {axis} edge at ({x}, {y}, {z}) mm. A tiny cell there makes the run slow; move or merge the copper edges near it in KiCad."
msgstr ""

#. E_UNUSED_PRIMITIVE
#, python-brace-format
msgid "openEMS left part of {property} out of the model ({type}). A primitive type such as Box touches no mesh edge, \"none\" means the property holds no primitive, and \"outside\" means it lies outside the simulated region. So that port or part is not in the model. Look at it with `preview`."
msgstr ""

#. W_UNUSED_PRIMITIVE
#, python-brace-format
msgid "openEMS left part of {property} out of the model ({type}). A primitive type such as LinPoly is a sliver smaller than a cell, \"none\" means the property holds no primitive, and \"outside\" means it lies outside the simulated region. Look at it with `preview` if it should carry current."
msgstr ""

#. E_METAL_IN_PML
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The model has metal, dielectric or a port within the PML or the 2 cells just inside its inner edge: along {axis} it reaches {at_mm} mm, past {limit_mm} mm. Copper or dielectric in the absorber makes the run unstable; widen the air gap around the board."
msgstr ""

#. W_GATE_LIMITS
#, python-brace-format
msgid "project.json sets gates.fit2d_limit {fit2d_limit} and gates.dt_floor {dt_floor}, not 0.03 and 0.8, so this verdict is outside the validated limits. Set them back to 0.03 and 0.8 for a validated result."
msgstr ""

#. I_GATES_PASSED
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Gates passed: edge lint, fit2d, timestep floor (dt {dt} s), port connectivity and unused primitives."
msgstr ""

#. I_GATES_PASSED_PML
